<Root>
  <DefaultMacro>
    <Major></Major>
    <Description>Auto attack macro for rogue in Diablo. This macro will help you auto-attack and auto-pickup.

- TO USE THIS MACRO -
1. Bind any key you want to use macro.
   Set the operating mode to "Run until pressed again".

2. Launch your game. Open the settings menu. Click the CONTROLS option.
   Go to 'Gameplay &gt; Combine Interact &amp; Skills' and tick it.

3. And then set "Force Move" to any key you want.
  *("Force Move" option will help you dodge automatically.)
  *(If you want to dodge manually, please ignore this step.)

4. Now everything is done. Just press your macro bindkey once.
   And hold your "Force Move" key to attack monsters automatically.

- NOTES -
1. You have to bind any key that does not conflict with other in-game keys for this macro.
2. If the macro gets glitched. You can just stop the macro and restart to solve it.</Description>
    <Comment></Comment>
    <GUIOption>
      <RepeatType>0</RepeatType>
    </GUIOption>
    <KeyUp>
      <Syntax></Syntax>
    </KeyUp>
    <KeyDown>
      <Syntax>LeftDown 1
Delay 25 ms
KeyDown 8 1
Delay 25 ms
LeftUp 1
Delay 25 ms
KeyUp 8 1
Delay 25 ms
RightDown 1
Delay 25 ms
RightUp 1
Delay 25 ms</Syntax>
    </KeyDown>
    <Software>Diablo 3</Software>
  </DefaultMacro>
</Root>